Subject: Borrow frame receivers for element stores

What this does
  Removes a local or argument receiver load on the store path, where the
  receiver is pushed before the key and value.

Why we need it
  The store pays the same duplicate, push, dispatch and release as the load, for
  a receiver the frame already owns.

What it adds
  The same window scan recognises a store whose receiver sits at the simulated
  depth below its key and value, admits nested element loads inside the window,
  and emits one combined store opcode that selects the local or argument register
  file from its operand. The receiver stays in its frame slot, the key and value
  are consumed exactly once, and the slow property path takes a real reference
  before it can run user code.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  Yes. The final series-wide bump remains in 9999.
